  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Energy Use Monitoring & Heat Optimization for a refinery's crude preheat train, FCC heat recovery, fired heaters, and waste heat boilers. Stakeholders include the Energy Manager (Solomon EII, energy cost, heat recovery), Refinery Manager (energy spend, fouling-driven margin loss), and Sustainability/ESG leadership (CO2 intensity, Scope 1 emissions).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Solomon EII = energy_efficiency_index; 100 = industry average, <85 = top-quartile target\n- Heat recovery = heat_recovery_pct on energy_kpi_monthly; world-class crude preheat trains exceed 85%\n- Thermal efficiency = thermal_efficiency_pct on energy_readings; modern fired heaters target 90%+\n- Fouling factor = fouling_factor; rising trend signals cleaning ROI vs. lost duty\n- UA ratio = actual_ua_btu_hr_f / clean_ua_btu_hr_f on thermal_snapshots; <0.7 typically triggers a cleaning case\n- Energy intensity = energy_intensity_btu_bbl; benchmark depends on configuration but ~80,000–120,000 BTU/bbl is competitive\n- CO2 intensity = co2_intensity_kg_bbl; refining industry average ~30 kg/bbl, best-in-class <20 kg/bbl\n- Energy cost = total_energy_cost_usd; typically the largest variable cost after feedstock\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - energy_readings_metrics (source: energy_readings) — dims: reading_date, exchanger_id, equipment_category, process_unit; measures: total_energy_mmbtu, avg_thermal_efficiency, avg_fouling_factor, avg_heat_duty, total_inlet_temp_f, total_outlet_temp_f, max_energy_consumption_mmbtu.\n  - thermal_snapshots_metrics (source: thermal_snapshots) — dims: snapshot_date, exchanger_id, equipment_category, process_unit; measures: avg_effectiveness_pct, avg_energy_intensity, total_co2_tons, avg_ua_ratio, max_clean_ua_btu_hr_f.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. exchanger_name, inlet_temp_f, outlet_temp_f, energy_efficiency_index, heat_recovery_pct, total_energy_cost_usd).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Top 10 exchangers by total energy consumption (MMBTU) over the last 12 months.",
    "Show monthly trend of average Solomon Energy Efficiency Index for the trailing 12 months.",
    "Which fired heaters have thermal efficiency below 70% and need tuning?",
    "Top 10 process units by total CO2 emissions year-to-date.",
    "Which heat exchangers have actual/clean UA ratio below 0.7 — candidates for cleaning?",
    "How has heat recovery percentage trended month-over-month across the crude preheat train?",
    "Which equipment categories have the highest average energy intensity per barrel?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "How has average inlet temperature trended by month?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_date, MEASURE(avg_inlet_temp_f) AS avg_inlet_temp_f",
        "FROM {fqn}.energy_readings_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY reading_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has average outlet temperature in fahrenheit trended over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_date, AVG(outlet_temp_f) AS avg_outlet_temp_f",
        "FROM {fqn}.energy_readings",
        "GROUP BY reading_date",
        "ORDER BY reading_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in average heat transfer effectiveness?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', snapshot_date) AS month, MEASURE(avg_effectiveness_pct) AS avg_effectiveness_pct",
        "FROM {fqn}.thermal_snapshots_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total energy consumption in mmbtu over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_date, SUM(energy_consumption_mmbtu) AS total_energy_consumption_mmbtu",
        "FROM {fqn}.energy_readings",
        "GROUP BY reading_date ORDER BY reading_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total clean ua value btu/hr/f trended over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, SUM(clean_ua_btu_hr_f) AS total_clean_ua_btu_hr_f",
        "FROM {fqn}.thermal_snapshots",
        "GROUP BY snapshot_date",
        "ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How does solomon energy efficiency index compare across equipment categorys?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT equipment_category, AVG(energy_efficiency_index) AS avg_energy_efficiency_index",
        "FROM {fqn}.energy_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY equipment_category",
        "ORDER BY equipment_category",
        "LIMIT 10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "Which heat exchangers have the best average inlet temperature in fahrenheit?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT exchanger_name, AVG(inlet_temp_f) AS avg_metric",
        "FROM {fqn}.energy_readings",
        "GROUP BY exchanger_name",
        "ORDER BY avg_metric DESC",
        "LIMIT 10"
      ]
    }
  ],
